no future in Poland.

00:24:56.959 --> 00:25:00.359
Here, we're one big family.

00:25:01.719 --> 00:25:04.800
We're going back to agriculture,
like in the Bible.

00:25:08.880 --> 00:25:11.160
Men and women,
we work all day

00:25:11.239 --> 00:25:13.359
while
our children are at daycare.

00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:23.839
In the kibbutz,
we are all equal,

00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:25.479
We share everything.

00:25:26.160 --> 00:25:28.239
Each person pays their salary to the community.

00:25:32.479 --> 00:25:34.599
and we make
all our decisions together.

00:25:45.760 --> 00:25:48.719
For these idealistic young people
who came from the far reaches of Europe,

00:25:49.760 --> 00:25:51.079
The experience is unique.

00:25:53.079 --> 00:25:54.280
With his classmates,

00:25:55.160 --> 00:25:59.359
Joël Iglinskiy simply intends to
build a different world.

00:26:05.280 --> 00:26:07.400
We have committed ourselves
to building socialism.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:11.959
The red flag
flies over the kibbutz.

00:26:14.719 --> 00:26:17.599
We admire Herzl,
Léon Blum and Marx.

00:26:18.640 --> 00:26:19.959
We are revolutionaries.

00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:22.359
And we know
that we're going to change the world.

00:26:38.839 --> 00:26:39.760
On site,

00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:44.119
The inhabitants who witnessed the arrival of the Jews wondered what was happening.

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:48.560
What do the Zionists want?

00:26:52.319 --> 00:26:54.400
How far will the colonization of land go?

00:27:00.079 --> 00:27:04.160
Why
do they come to Palestine?

00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:10.959
In the 1930s,

00:27:11.640 --> 00:27:14.599
The Arabs of Palestine
number one million.

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:18.400
They represent
two-thirds of the population

00:27:18.479 --> 00:27:20.880
and are distributed
throughout the territory

00:27:21.439 --> 00:27:23.719
in hundreds
of towns and villages.

00:27:29.199 --> 00:27:30.839
They are called
the Palestinians

00:27:31.520 --> 00:27:35.280
in memory of the Philistine people of antiquity.

00:27:38.880 --> 00:27:43.359
Before the arrival of the British,
they lived under the Turkish empire.

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:45.000
for four centuries.

00:27:49.079 --> 00:27:52.160
Look at these color images
shot at the beginning of the 20th century.

00:27:53.400 --> 00:27:56.920
Their Eastern culture
has always fascinated visitors.

00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:04.920
Some of them are Bedouins.

00:28:06.079 --> 00:28:08.640
They live in the desert
with their herds,

00:28:15.160 --> 00:28:16.719
but most of them
are farmers.

00:28:18.400 --> 00:28:20.959
They work
for large Arab landowners,

00:28:21.040 --> 00:28:23.599
like here,
on the coastal plain,

00:28:23.800 --> 00:28:26.520
where the famous Jaffa oranges are produced.

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:31.839
They are exported
all over the world.

00:28:38.359 --> 00:28:40.079
For several years now,

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:46.280
Some Arab landowners agree
to sell their land to the Zionists.

00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:56.839
And little by little,
the face of Palestine is changing.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:06.280
By 1935, Jews already represented 30% of the population.

00:29:06.560 --> 00:29:10.880
They created dozens of villages along the coast and to the north.

00:29:16.400 --> 00:29:18.800
This does not prevent
most Arab families

00:29:18.880 --> 00:29:22.520
to live
the pre-war years without suspicion

00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:24.560
and in
a certain happiness.

00:29:27.239 --> 00:29:30.719
This is the case,
in Jerusalem, of the Said family.

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:34.640
Christian Arabs,
who own a publishing house.

00:29:39.239 --> 00:29:41.599
Filmed by his father
during the summer holidays,

00:29:42.040 --> 00:29:43.839
This boy's name is Edward.

00:29:45.680 --> 00:29:49.079
This is the future
Palestinian writer Edward Said.

00:29:52.040 --> 00:29:54.520
Our family home
was located in Talbiya,

00:29:55.280 --> 00:29:57.839
a neighborhood
of Christian Palestinians like us.

00:30:01.599 --> 00:30:04.959
The imposing two-story villa
had many bedrooms

00:30:06.079 --> 00:30:09.280
and a lovely garden in which
my two youngest cousins,

00:30:09.599 --> 00:30:11.280
My sisters and I could play.

00:30:14.359 --> 00:30:16.920
It was
an idyllic time.

00:30:19.199 --> 00:30:21.199
In their family film,

00:30:21.400 --> 00:30:24.280
nothing yet suggests
that this idyllic period

00:30:24.359 --> 00:30:26.079
is about to end.

00:30:32.880 --> 00:30:33.880
At the same time,

00:30:35.359 --> 00:30:36.199
in Germany.

00:30:37.800 --> 00:30:41.599
The situation is becoming
dramatic for the Jews.

00:30:46.680 --> 00:30:50.599
The Nazis who sought
to create an ethnically pure country,

00:30:50.920 --> 00:30:52.680
multiply
the provocations

00:30:54.319 --> 00:30:58.000
and anti-Semitic graffiti is spreading throughout the country.

00:31:03.680 --> 00:31:04.760
On the trams

00:31:06.319 --> 00:31:09.479
and even
on public benches.

00:31:16.599 --> 00:31:19.839
At the congress
of Nuremberg in 1935,

00:31:20.760 --> 00:31:26.359
The Nazis officially excluded
Jews from the national community.

00:31:46.239 --> 00:31:50.479
Among German Jews,
panic is beginning to set in.

00:31:51.880 --> 00:31:55.719
And more and more people are seeking to flee abroad.

00:31:55.800 --> 00:32:00.079
to France,
Great Britain or the United States.

00:32:01.359 --> 00:32:05.160
This is where a Jewish community of 4 million people already lives.

00:32:10.920 --> 00:32:14.640
But visas for Western countries
are granted sparingly.

00:32:17.760 --> 00:32:22.479
Thus, more than 100,000 German Jews
chose Palestine

00:32:23.599 --> 00:32:26.880
where the doors of immigration
are still open to them.

00:32:32.439 --> 00:32:35.160
Around one hundred Jewish families
arrive in Palestine

00:32:35.239 --> 00:32:38.640
aboard the Mariette Pacha,
of the Compagnie des Messageries Maritimes.

00:32:38.800 --> 00:32:41.160
Most of them
are in a state of absolute destitution,

00:32:41.239 --> 00:32:45.280
Reich laws prohibiting
Jews from transferring their property.

00:32:45.400 --> 00:32:48.119
Zionist associations
are welcoming these unfortunate people

00:32:48.280 --> 00:32:50.640
and give them
the means to rebuild their lives.

00:32:58.079 --> 00:33:01.359
Among the passengers
of the Mariette Pacha were the Weilers,

00:33:02.119 --> 00:33:04.119
our Jewish family from Berlin.

00:33:07.520 --> 00:33:12.439
Unlike the other passengers,
the Weilers are simply visitors.

00:33:13.280 --> 00:33:15.920
Without yet knowing
if they will settle in Palestine

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:20.400
with their two little girls
and leave Germany for good.

00:33:28.359 --> 00:33:31.199
They continue filming
with their personal camera.

00:33:35.119 --> 00:33:39.239
To convince his wife,
Friedrich Weiler took her on a tour of the country.

00:33:40.239 --> 00:33:42.439
He takes her
to the shores of the Dead Sea.

00:33:49.119 --> 00:33:54.119
They are visiting Tel Aviv,
this Jewish metropolis of 130,000 inhabitants

00:33:54.199 --> 00:33:56.199
built from the ground
in less than 20 years.

00:34:00.920 --> 00:34:04.599
They are visiting German friends who have already settled there.

00:34:08.919 --> 00:34:09.879
Yet,

00:34:10.360 --> 00:34:15.560
After a week of travel,
they are still hesitant to take the plunge.

00:34:23.479 --> 00:34:24.520
In Jerusalem,

00:34:25.120 --> 00:34:27.600
They found
a city in turmoil,

00:34:29.520 --> 00:34:30.600
close to revolt.

00:34:39.479 --> 00:34:41.040
At the call of the Grand Mufti,

00:34:41.959 --> 00:34:45.520
Palestinian Arabs demonstrate against the British occupation.

00:34:46.399 --> 00:34:49.360
and its favorable policy
to the mass arrival of Jews.

00:34:56.239 --> 00:34:58.280
One of their spokespeople explains.

00:35:39.679 --> 00:35:41.919
Since the beginning of the 1930s,

00:35:42.719 --> 00:35:45.719
Demonstrations
continue in Palestine.

00:35:46.399 --> 00:35:48.159
Increasingly violent.

00:35:52.040 --> 00:35:54.320
Attacks
against the kibbutzim,

00:35:57.439 --> 00:35:59.360
attacks
in the middle of the street.

00:36:01.479 --> 00:36:07.280
In 1936, what is known as
the great Arab revolt finally broke out.

00:36:09.399 --> 00:36:11.959
One of its leaders
is named Fawzi al-Qawuqji.

00:36:13.959 --> 00:36:16.360
He launches a guerrilla war
against the British army.

00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:20.959
We are rebelling
against injustices,

00:36:22.840 --> 00:36:24.080
against Zionism,

00:36:25.520 --> 00:36:27.360
to defend
our Holy Land.

00:36:29.600 --> 00:36:31.560
The English
abused Arab blood.

00:36:34.560 --> 00:36:36.959
Today,
we are ready to face them.

00:36:40.639 --> 00:36:44.239
The revolt spreads
within a few months to all of Palestine

00:36:45.320 --> 00:36:48.040
and it forces
the British to send reinforcements.

00:37:01.760 --> 00:37:03.239
The repression is relentless.

00:37:04.399 --> 00:37:11.320
As here in Jaffa, where a neighborhood
is emptied of its inhabitants and razed.

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:23.439
It took the British army two years
to quell the revolt,

00:37:24.919 --> 00:37:26.439
but this is
only temporary.

00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:32.360
In 1938,

00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:35.600
on one of the Arab peasants taken prisoner,

00:37:36.879 --> 00:37:41.320
We find a leaflet;
it sounds like a warning.

00:37:44.199 --> 00:37:49.000
Today, you are cruelly trying
to strip us of our rights,

00:37:50.239 --> 00:37:51.080
from our homes,

00:37:52.439 --> 00:37:53.439
of our honor.

00:37:56.320 --> 00:38:01.360
Know that never,
before we have won our freedom,

00:38:03.199 --> 00:38:04.639
We will not surrender our weapons.

00:38:16.159 --> 00:38:18.800
The same year,
in Germany.

00:38:22.679 --> 00:38:25.159
It is
November 9, 1938.

00:38:28.840 --> 00:38:32.000
In front of the public
who observe and sometimes approve,

00:38:33.399 --> 00:38:36.199
The Nazis set fire to
Jewish places of worship.

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:49.040
It's Kristallnacht.

00:38:52.239 --> 00:38:56.760
A massive pogrom during which
8,000 shops were looted

00:38:57.520 --> 00:38:59.520
and about a hundred
Jews murdered.

00:39:11.399 --> 00:39:12.520
A few months earlier,

00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:18.840
Germany took control
of Austria, where 200,000 Jews lived.

00:39:25.560 --> 00:39:28.040
In a new wave of antisemitism,

00:39:28.800 --> 00:39:31.679
Tensions are rising sharply in Europe.

00:39:33.320 --> 00:39:36.239
and the risk of a new world war is drawing closer.

00:39:42.600 --> 00:39:45.360
Some European Jews
realize that for them,

00:39:46.719 --> 00:39:48.719
The countdown has begun.

00:39:59.800 --> 00:40:01.679
Shortly before Kristallnacht,

00:40:02.080 --> 00:40:06.320
The Weilers have made the decision
to leave Berlin permanently

00:40:07.000 --> 00:40:08.320
and to emigrate to Palestine.

00:40:10.919 --> 00:40:15.719
In the photos taken before departure,
the parents are trying to put on a brave face,

00:40:16.600 --> 00:40:19.280
But Friedrich notes in his diary:

00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:23.760
"We are spending the last few days
in fear."

00:40:25.719 --> 00:40:27.959
"Until the very end
I feared the Gestapo"

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:30.760
"requires
an additional formality from us."

00:40:32.239 --> 00:40:36.560
"On the last night, my mother
felt like she was suffocating at the thought of our departure."

00:40:40.719 --> 00:40:45.600
Friedrich's mother, Ida,
decided to stay in Germany.

00:40:47.399 --> 00:40:49.560
She tries to reassure
her little girls.

00:40:52.760 --> 00:40:56.560
The Nazis,
there's no need to worry.

00:40:58.159 --> 00:41:00.159
We only have them for a while.

00:41:00.919 --> 00:41:05.239
All of this, you'll see,
it will pass.

00:41:13.120 --> 00:41:16.600
Berlin,
the day of departure.

00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:23.159
The parents
take some final photos on the platform.

00:41:26.199 --> 00:41:29.560
Grandmother Ida came to say goodbye to the whole family.

00:41:31.399 --> 00:41:35.520
Ella, his little girl,
here on the right, is enthusiastic.

00:41:37.959 --> 00:41:41.439
She doesn't realize that she is seeing her grandmother for the last time.

00:41:44.479 --> 00:41:46.479
I'm excited about this trip.

00:41:47.679 --> 00:41:49.679
It's a new life
that begins.

00:41:53.520 --> 00:41:57.479
We are crossing Austria
where Hitler has just seized power.

00:41:59.560 --> 00:42:01.040
We cross the Alps.

00:42:01.719 --> 00:42:04.600
This is the first time
I've seen such large mountains.

00:42:08.520 --> 00:42:10.840
And then, there we were,
we found ourselves in Italy.

00:42:13.439 --> 00:42:16.000
The Nazis,
with their wickedness, are behind us.

00:42:24.840 --> 00:42:27.679
The family embarked
for Palestine.

00:42:32.000 --> 00:42:34.120
Our boat
is called the Jerusalem.

00:42:36.639 --> 00:42:38.800
To pass the time,
Mom knits

00:42:43.639 --> 00:42:46.320
And me,
I read books all day.

00:42:58.520 --> 00:43:02.679
After five days at sea,
the Weilers landed in Palestine.

00:43:04.520 --> 00:43:09.159
The parents chose to settle
in a small house north of Tel Aviv

00:43:10.439 --> 00:43:14.199
where they believe their two daughters
will be able to grow up in safety.

00:43:16.639 --> 00:43:19.560
They will soon learn
that they are among the last

00:43:19.879 --> 00:43:22.239
to have been able to
reach Palestine.

00:43:29.040 --> 00:43:30.800
Because in the spring of 1939,

00:43:32.280 --> 00:43:34.959
The situation
changed abruptly.

00:43:38.679 --> 00:43:41.639
Great Britain,
which still occupies Palestine,

00:43:42.320 --> 00:43:44.840
makes a decision
that changes everything.

00:43:50.439 --> 00:43:54.479
To secure the support of the Arabs
in the next war against Hitler,

00:43:56.280 --> 00:43:59.800
The British decide
to cease supporting Zionism.

00:44:02.000 --> 00:44:04.560
To limit the number
of entry visas for Jews

00:44:06.439 --> 00:44:08.439
as well as land purchases.

00:44:11.800 --> 00:44:14.239
A catastrophic decision for the Zionists.

00:44:14.840 --> 00:44:17.719
who planned to force millions of Jews to emigrate from Europe

00:44:17.840 --> 00:44:19.600
before the outbreak of war.

00:44:21.719 --> 00:44:23.520
Their leader in Palestine,

00:44:23.600 --> 00:44:28.479
David Ben-Gurion,
in turn, chose to force the issue.

00:44:34.479 --> 00:44:38.159
He decides to accelerate
the tower and palisade operations,

00:44:39.120 --> 00:44:40.520
these colony creations

00:44:40.600 --> 00:44:43.000
which have multiplied in previous years

00:44:43.639 --> 00:44:45.639
and which rely
on the element of surprise.

00:44:48.159 --> 00:44:53.679
It is July 12, 1939,
in Negba, near the Negev desert.

00:44:57.280 --> 00:44:59.639
Zionist militants
charged at a convoy

00:44:59.760 --> 00:45:03.320
prefabricated houses
that they are going to install here.

00:45:04.760 --> 00:45:07.959
On these lands
which they had previously bought from the Arabs.

00:45:10.679 --> 00:45:12.800
Among them
is Joel Iglinskiy.

00:45:16.080 --> 00:45:17.159
"We need to move quickly."

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:21.000
"Everyone knows what they have to do."

00:45:22.800 --> 00:45:26.560
"We erect fences by putting
gravel inside the planks"

00:45:27.719 --> 00:45:29.120
"To stop the bullets."

00:45:33.120 --> 00:45:34.520
"We're going up
the watchtower."

00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:38.360
"We forget about the fatigue"

00:45:43.040 --> 00:45:45.760
"because we are
the soldiers of the Zionist revolution"

00:45:49.159 --> 00:45:52.719
"And we know we're doing something bigger than ourselves."

00:46:03.560 --> 00:46:08.399
In the summer of 1939,
as the impending cataclysm approached,

00:46:09.159 --> 00:46:11.159
The Jews are holding their breath.

00:46:13.000 --> 00:46:15.040
Some,
as we have shown,

00:46:15.239 --> 00:46:18.439
sought refuge
by emigrating to Palestine.

00:46:20.040 --> 00:46:24.879
Others still hope to continue
living in Europe despite the danger.

00:46:28.280 --> 00:46:32.560
It will only take them a few months
to achieve the unimaginable.

00:46:34.399 --> 00:46:38.040
The Nazis' plan to destroy
an entire people.

00:46:40.800 --> 00:46:44.159
This is the new chapter
that we are now going to tell you about.

00:47:01.280 --> 00:47:03.399
September 1, 1939,

00:47:04.560 --> 00:47:06.600
Germany invaded Poland.

00:47:10.000 --> 00:47:12.479
This is the beginning
of the Second World War.

00:47:16.560 --> 00:47:21.000
From the very first weeks,
the Nazis, who crushed the Polish army,

00:47:21.080 --> 00:47:22.719
they are increasing their abuses.

00:47:27.959 --> 00:47:29.560
Forced labor

00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:31.520
blows,

00:47:32.840 --> 00:47:33.919
humiliations,

00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:40.600
as dozens of photos taken across the country show,

00:47:41.280 --> 00:47:44.000
German soldiers
unleashed their fury against the Jews.

00:47:50.520 --> 00:47:53.760
Hitler ordered
the roundup of Polish Jews,

00:47:54.120 --> 00:47:59.040
men, women, and children,
in quarters reserved for them,

00:48:05.600 --> 00:48:06.760
the ghettos.

00:48:15.120 --> 00:48:20.000
The Nazis chose to isolate
their future victims from the rest of the world,

00:48:24.199 --> 00:48:25.719
to starve them little by little,

00:48:29.159 --> 00:48:32.600
before, soon, deciding
to murder them en masse, here.

00:48:44.239 --> 00:48:47.560
The massacre begins
a year and a half later,

00:48:48.199 --> 00:48:50.439
June 22, 1941,

00:48:51.600 --> 00:48:53.719
when the German army
attacked the USSR.

00:48:59.600 --> 00:49:02.600
A lightning offensive which,
in just a few days,

00:49:02.679 --> 00:49:05.600
pushes the Soviets back
for hundreds of kilometers.

00:49:13.600 --> 00:49:15.239
In the conquered cities,

00:49:15.320 --> 00:49:18.840
The Nazis immediately launched
the persecution of the Jews

00:49:20.639 --> 00:49:23.080
by getting help
from the population.

00:49:32.639 --> 00:49:35.280
Everywhere, like here in Zloczow,

00:49:36.679 --> 00:49:38.600
pro-German nationalists

00:49:38.760 --> 00:49:42.040
far-right activists
and convicted criminals

00:49:42.159 --> 00:49:45.919
launch pogroms
under the encouragement of the Germans.

00:49:51.639 --> 00:49:54.719
They accuse the Jews
of being responsible for massacres

00:49:54.879 --> 00:49:58.000
which were committed by the Soviets
a few days earlier.

00:50:04.600 --> 00:50:06.560
In Lviv, Ukraine,

00:50:07.840 --> 00:50:11.040
A German soldier films the crowd
and the Ukrainian militiamen.

00:50:16.840 --> 00:50:18.320
Dozens
of Jewish women,

00:50:18.600 --> 00:50:22.520
After being raped,
they will be murdered along with their families.

00:50:30.719 --> 00:50:35.560
An SS sergeant, Félix Landau,
who was nevertheless fiercely anti-Semitic,

00:50:36.199 --> 00:50:38.399
is surprised
by this outburst of violence.

00:50:41.919 --> 00:50:44.919
"We see things that are almost impossible to describe."

00:50:46.679 --> 00:50:49.320
"Hundreds
of Jews covered in blood,"

00:50:49.959 --> 00:50:51.199
"holes in the head,"

00:50:52.479 --> 00:50:53.520
"broken hands"

00:50:56.639 --> 00:50:58.840
"and the eyes dangling
out of their sockets"

00:51:00.479 --> 00:51:01.560
"are being beaten up"

00:51:03.800 --> 00:51:04.800
"of hatred"

00:51:07.120 --> 00:51:07.959
"and rage."

00:51:14.879 --> 00:51:19.120
Within hours, the massacre
spread to dozens of cities.

00:51:24.199 --> 00:51:25.719
Still on July 4th,

00:51:26.360 --> 00:51:29.800
The Germans are approaching Kaunas in Lithuania.

00:51:39.239 --> 00:51:41.679
This is where Dita Katz and her entire family live.

00:51:43.560 --> 00:51:47.520
Do you remember that film
shot twelve years earlier, in 1929?

00:51:49.479 --> 00:51:53.639
When the Germans arrived, the grandfather
tried to reassure his family.

00:51:57.719 --> 00:51:59.360
"Don't be afraid of the Germans."

00:51:59.959 --> 00:52:02.639
"I knew them
during the First World War."

00:52:03.239 --> 00:52:04.760
"They are civilized people."

00:52:09.280 --> 00:52:11.520
However,
from the very first hours,

00:52:12.199 --> 00:52:16.040
His own son, Itzhak,
disappears around a street corner.

00:52:17.879 --> 00:52:21.360
The rest,
