01:20:23.040 --> 01:20:25.439
"Our dream is
becoming a reality."

01:20:27.439 --> 01:20:29.439
"The Jewish state
is getting closer to us."

01:20:31.040 --> 01:20:32.439
"It's fantastic."

01:20:34.680 --> 01:20:36.879
"We dance,
we laugh, we sing."

01:20:38.359 --> 01:20:40.600
"Everyone
kisses each other without knowing each other."

01:20:41.959 --> 01:20:43.040
"What joy!"

01:20:51.759 --> 01:20:53.919
They crossed the borders clandestinely.

01:20:55.439 --> 01:20:58.240
They reached their promised land
on makeshift ships,

01:21:00.120 --> 01:21:03.560
They now have the support of the international community.

01:21:06.040 --> 01:21:10.479
At the end of 1947,
the Zionists seemed close to their goal.

01:21:12.319 --> 01:21:15.359
Will the two peoples now be able to reach an agreement?

01:21:19.759 --> 01:21:20.680
According to the UN,

01:21:21.560 --> 01:21:24.799
The partition
must be followed by two separate states,

01:21:26.120 --> 01:21:28.640
One was Jewish,
the other Arab.

01:21:35.000 --> 01:21:36.520
We will explain to you

01:21:36.600 --> 01:21:39.680
Why did this project collapse in just six months?

01:21:41.479 --> 01:21:46.240
and how the creation of Israel plunged
the Arabs of Palestine into misfortune

01:21:46.680 --> 01:21:49.000
and exile
for decades.

01:22:01.839 --> 01:22:05.439
November 30, 1947,
the day after the UN vote.

01:22:08.080 --> 01:22:12.680
A young Arab woman from Jaffa,
Afif Elkouri, is outraged.

01:22:16.160 --> 01:22:18.520
"Why should we give away half the country?"

01:22:19.319 --> 01:22:21.240
"So that they can make it
a Jewish state?"

01:22:25.359 --> 01:22:27.160
"And what will become of the non-Jews?"

01:22:29.479 --> 01:22:32.839
"Now,
there is only one solution left: to fight."

01:22:36.640 --> 01:22:38.120
To defend their rights,

01:22:38.879 --> 01:22:42.040
Thousands of peasants
join the guerrilla war.

01:22:48.439 --> 01:22:50.479
One of their leaders
is Fawzi al-Qawuqji.

01:22:51.359 --> 01:22:55.120
One of the heroes
of the great Arab revolt of 1936.

01:22:57.040 --> 01:23:00.000
He only has a few weeks
to train his troops.

01:23:04.640 --> 01:23:08.240
"My soldiers only have basic weapons
that they bought themselves."

01:23:13.879 --> 01:23:18.240
"We sent SOS signals to neighboring Arab countries, but in vain."

01:23:20.479 --> 01:23:23.720
"Yet, the hatred is so intense
that one is ready to sacrifice oneself."

01:23:30.200 --> 01:23:31.600
In the opposing camp,

01:23:32.240 --> 01:23:37.120
The Haganah, Israel's future army,
has been training for months.

01:23:41.160 --> 01:23:44.120
Surrounded by World War II veterans,

01:23:46.839 --> 01:23:49.399
It is made up of
highly motivated young recruits.

01:23:56.120 --> 01:24:00.399
Among them, Zvi Katz,
here, on the right of the photo.

01:24:02.839 --> 01:24:06.080
He escaped from the Cyprus camp
thanks to an underground network.

01:24:09.640 --> 01:24:11.040
"I only think about fighting."

01:24:13.399 --> 01:24:15.879
"For us,
it's a matter of dignity."

01:24:19.279 --> 01:24:22.919
"We no longer want to be like
animals who are killed without saying a word."

01:24:25.479 --> 01:24:28.479
"Never again will we allow ourselves to be slaughtered like sheep."

01:24:32.240 --> 01:24:35.839
The two young Berliners,
Ella and Bärbel Weiler,

01:24:36.000 --> 01:24:38.279
They, too,
joined the Haganah.

01:24:41.640 --> 01:24:42.600
They have just learned

01:24:42.680 --> 01:24:45.359
that their grandmother died
during the war in Poland,

01:24:45.959 --> 01:24:47.439
murdered by the Nazis

01:24:50.399 --> 01:24:52.200
They are determined.

01:24:53.879 --> 01:24:57.279
"During the war,
no one acted to save the Jews."

01:24:59.279 --> 01:25:02.799
"Today,
we can only rely on ourselves."

01:25:05.759 --> 01:25:10.000
"If we don't help ourselves, who will help us?"

01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:16.680
In the spring of 1948,

01:25:18.160 --> 01:25:20.759
Fawzi al-Qawuqji
and other Arab leaders

01:25:20.919 --> 01:25:23.560
launch their troops
to assault the Jewish positions.

01:25:27.759 --> 01:25:30.720
One of the targets
is Kibbutz Mishmar Haemek,

01:25:32.000 --> 01:25:34.479
the crossing point
from Galilee to Tel Aviv.

01:25:38.399 --> 01:25:41.439
"We start at 5 a.m.,
on the Jewish Sabbath."

01:25:48.560 --> 01:25:49.919
"I give the order
to fire the cannon"

01:25:49.959 --> 01:25:53.680
"to destroy as many houses as possible."

01:25:53.720 --> 01:25:55.879
"They seem to have suffered heavy losses."

01:26:03.879 --> 01:26:07.279
Opposite them, the defenders of the kibbutz
respond blow for blow.

01:26:16.959 --> 01:26:20.200
One of them,
Joël Lotan, is filming the fights.

01:26:24.200 --> 01:26:25.839
"We are trying
to repel the enemy."

01:26:29.560 --> 01:26:32.120
"And we hope to hold out
until reinforcements arrive."

01:26:35.479 --> 01:26:38.120
"Fortunately,
after a few days,"

01:26:38.600 --> 01:26:42.799
"Haganah soldiers eventually reached us from the hills,"

01:26:44.120 --> 01:26:45.759
"From Haifa."

01:26:55.319 --> 01:26:58.279
Within days,
Palestine was engulfed in flames.

01:27:06.000 --> 01:27:08.720
Offensive,
counter-offensive,

01:27:11.040 --> 01:27:14.279
the Haganah,
better organized than the Arab army,

01:27:14.839 --> 01:27:17.680
manages to gain the upper hand
from the very first weeks

01:27:17.959 --> 01:27:19.839
and to take
thousands of prisoners.

01:27:25.759 --> 01:27:29.279
In the conquered cities,
the population is becoming frightened

01:27:30.080 --> 01:27:32.080
and is considering
fleeing the fighting.

01:27:35.560 --> 01:27:39.319
On April 9, 1948,
an event reinforced these fears.

01:27:40.640 --> 01:27:47.560
In Deir Yassin, Jewish extremists massacred nearly 200 Arab villagers.

01:27:48.600 --> 01:27:49.879
including children.

01:27:51.279 --> 01:27:53.640
A massacre
of which no images remain,

01:27:53.720 --> 01:27:55.879
but whose news
is spreading around the world

01:27:56.640 --> 01:27:58.160
and triggers panic.

01:28:02.359 --> 01:28:05.279
In Jaffa,
a few rare photos taken on the spot

01:28:06.000 --> 01:28:08.680
show the residents
who are abandoning their homes

01:28:09.279 --> 01:28:10.479
and leave the city.

01:28:11.919 --> 01:28:13.919
Among them
is Youssef Chaker.

01:28:19.160 --> 01:28:21.919
"We heard about Deir Yassin on the radio."

01:28:24.080 --> 01:28:27.240
"We heard that the Arab countries
were going to come to our aid."

01:28:29.720 --> 01:28:31.720
"In the meantime,
we prefer to leave."

01:28:34.359 --> 01:28:39.479
"I get into a truck, we pile in
and we head towards Beirut."

01:28:41.439 --> 01:28:43.520
This is the beginning
of the Palestinian exodus.

01:28:46.680 --> 01:28:49.600
A few streets away
is Afif Elkouri.

01:28:53.680 --> 01:28:55.680
"The whole city is
fleeing."

01:28:59.479 --> 01:29:02.759
"On Arabic radio, they tell us
that we'll be back in two weeks,"

01:29:04.160 --> 01:29:05.919
"But
is that really true?"

01:29:09.359 --> 01:29:12.560
Those who fled will never be allowed to return home.

01:29:14.919 --> 01:29:19.080
Now, the city of Jaffa,
deserted by its inhabitants,

01:29:19.720 --> 01:29:22.720
will be officially considered
an Israeli city.

01:29:38.240 --> 01:29:42.080
May 14, 1948,
the day everything changed.

01:29:46.279 --> 01:29:48.560
It is 10 a.m.
at the port of Haifa.

01:29:50.720 --> 01:29:55.200
British Governor Alan Cunningham
is embarking for England.

01:30:03.080 --> 01:30:07.560
Britain ends three decades of presence in Palestine

01:30:08.359 --> 01:30:10.439
and leaves
the two sides facing each other.

01:30:17.759 --> 01:30:20.399
Six hours later, in Tel Aviv,

01:30:21.520 --> 01:30:26.080
The leader of the Zionists, David Ben-Gurion,
decided to proclaim the Jewish state.

01:31:01.799 --> 01:31:03.319
After
years of struggle,

01:31:04.799 --> 01:31:07.399
The Zionists
are reconnecting with Jewish history.

01:31:13.319 --> 01:31:17.279
Behind their flag will rally
a minority of Palestinian Arabs.

01:31:19.799 --> 01:31:23.240
150,000 people
who choose to stay put

01:31:23.839 --> 01:31:26.359
and who will become Israeli citizens.

01:31:28.160 --> 01:31:34.839
Today,
60 years later, they represent 20% of the population.

01:31:45.879 --> 01:31:48.919
But most
of the Palestinian Arabs take to the road.

01:31:50.919 --> 01:31:53.000
It's almost
an entire people,

01:31:53.200 --> 01:31:57.319
Men, women and children,
who are now fleeing abroad.

01:32:00.359 --> 01:32:03.680
It is called the Nakba,
the catastrophe in Arabic.

01:32:06.879 --> 01:32:10.839
The exodus that began in April
after the Deir Yassin massacre,

01:32:11.399 --> 01:32:13.520
will affect
more than 700,000 people.

01:32:14.080 --> 01:32:16.080
Two-thirds
of the Arab population.

01:32:27.080 --> 01:32:30.080
Seven Arab countries declare war on Israel

01:32:30.680 --> 01:32:32.799
the day after
Ben-Gurion's speech,

01:32:33.160 --> 01:32:34.640
It changes nothing
about their fate.

01:32:37.520 --> 01:32:41.759
After several weeks of battle and
the capture of the Old City of Jerusalem,

01:32:42.640 --> 01:32:44.879
after several
spectacular advances,

01:32:46.479 --> 01:32:51.640
The Arab armies are retreating
and losing more territory.

01:33:02.240 --> 01:33:05.680
This situation further increases the flow of Palestinian refugees.

01:33:07.600 --> 01:33:10.799
According to the latest historical research
conducted in Israel,

01:33:11.600 --> 01:33:14.040
half
were allegedly forcibly expelled

01:33:14.799 --> 01:33:16.560
by Israeli soldiers.

01:33:22.560 --> 01:33:25.319
They found refuge
in neighboring Arab countries,

01:33:25.560 --> 01:33:29.720
in Jordan or Lebanon,
in refugee camps.

01:33:38.759 --> 01:33:42.919
Among them
is Abu Hicham, 19 years old.

01:33:48.399 --> 01:33:51.160
"We were given tents."

01:33:52.040 --> 01:33:53.319
"The ground is soaked."

01:33:56.080 --> 01:33:57.359
"We no longer have a country."

01:34:00.120 --> 01:34:01.959
"We can no longer
live normally."

01:34:04.759 --> 01:34:07.240
"We are being given
bread and cheese."

01:34:10.799 --> 01:34:13.640
"I feel humiliated
and I can only think of one thing,"

01:34:14.799 --> 01:34:16.240
"to return to my village."

01:34:19.640 --> 01:34:23.439
"For as long as it takes,
we will fight."

01:34:27.640 --> 01:34:28.479
Hate,

01:34:29.640 --> 01:34:30.600
humiliation,

01:34:32.040 --> 01:34:32.919
exile.

01:34:35.439 --> 01:34:36.799
In 1948,

01:34:37.919 --> 01:34:40.279
the history
of the Israeli-Arab conflict

01:34:40.680 --> 01:34:42.040
This is just the beginning.

01:34:55.759 --> 01:35:01.640
Today, Abu Hicham, 78,
still has refugee status.

01:35:03.959 --> 01:35:07.759
He lives in a Palestinian camp
in the suburbs of Beirut, Lebanon,

01:35:08.759 --> 01:35:10.759
a few kilometers
from Afif Elkouri.

01:35:13.680 --> 01:35:14.720
For 60 years,

01:35:15.640 --> 01:35:20.600
Neither of them was allowed
to return to live in their native land,

01:35:21.040 --> 01:35:22.120
Palestine.

01:35:26.959 --> 01:35:28.919
Some emigrated to the West,

01:35:29.720 --> 01:35:33.319
like Edward Said,
the little Arab Christian from Jerusalem.

01:35:36.319 --> 01:35:38.640
He became a university professor
in New York,

01:35:40.359 --> 01:35:45.040
Edward Said was one of the most famous spokespeople for the Palestinian people.

01:35:46.600 --> 01:35:48.600
until his death in 2003.

01:35:55.160 --> 01:35:59.600
On the other side, in Israel,
they all tried to rebuild their lives

01:36:00.439 --> 01:36:03.120
despite the trauma
of the Second World War.

01:36:05.799 --> 01:36:12.200
Mickaël Arens, the young Zionist from Riga,
dedicated himself to agriculture in Galilee.

01:36:18.120 --> 01:36:20.560
Deeply affected
by her childhood memories,

01:36:21.600 --> 01:36:28.399
Berliner Ella Weiler married
a Jewish man who, like her, came from Germany.

01:36:32.759 --> 01:36:34.759
They had
two children.

01:36:39.439 --> 01:36:41.319
His sister, Bärbel,

01:36:41.680 --> 01:36:45.640
She married a Polish Auschwitz survivor.

01:36:50.000 --> 01:36:51.959
She lives with him
in Tel Aviv.

01:36:53.160 --> 01:36:56.319
Grateful to her father,
who died in the 1960s,

01:36:57.160 --> 01:37:00.640
for having made him leave Germany
when there was still time.

01:37:04.439 --> 01:37:09.399
It was only in 1972 that Dita Katz
left Lithuania for Israel.

01:37:14.160 --> 01:37:18.200
There she was reunited with her brother Zvi,
who had become a reserve officer.

01:37:20.479 --> 01:37:24.759
They live in Tel Aviv
in the memory of their loved ones

01:37:24.839 --> 01:37:26.319
murdered by the Nazis.

01:37:30.160 --> 01:37:32.799
Perhaps the most surprising is
Joel Iglinskiy.

01:37:35.560 --> 01:37:39.600
At 99 years old,
he still lives in Nekbah,

01:37:39.680 --> 01:37:42.160
the kibbutz
which he created in 1939.

01:37:44.879 --> 01:37:51.839
More than ever, he remains faithful
to the socialist ideal of his youth.

